# ==========================================================================
#  ALLOWLIST, not a denylist.
#
#  Everything is ignored by default; only the tooling is added back. A
#  denylist fails open - one unmatched pattern and 75 MB of paid course
#  captures are in a commit and in the history forever. This direction fails
#  closed: a new file is invisible until someone deliberately un-ignores it.
#
#  If you add a file and git does not see it, that is this file working.
#  Check with:  git check-ignore -v <path>
# ==========================================================================

*

# --- the tooling ---------------------------------------------------------
!.gitignore
!.gitattributes
!README.md
!START HERE.md
!LICENSE
!PRISM - Mac.command
!PRISM - Windows.cmd
!scripts/
!scripts/*.py
!scripts/*.js
!scripts/*.md
!scripts/VERSION.json
!scripts/UPDATE_MANIFEST.json
!scripts/project_state.template.json
!control_center/
!control_center/**

# --- how the application is built, and by what ---------------------------
#  packaging/ is publisher build tooling only. It is deliberately outside
#  scripts/UPDATE_MANIFEST.json, so it never lands in a user's workspace.
!packaging/
!packaging/*.py
!packaging/*.txt
!packaging/*.md
!.github/
!.github/**

# --- folder skeleton, so a clone has the right shape ---------------------
!Source Files/
!Anki Decks/
!COMPLETED/
!work/
!*/.gitkeep
!Source Files/README.md
!Anki Decks/README.md
!COMPLETED/README.md

# --- the redacted worked example (invented content, safe to publish) -----
!COMPLETED/EXAMPLE/
!COMPLETED/EXAMPLE/**

# --- never, under any circumstances --------------------------------------
#  Belt and braces. The bare `*` above already covers these; they are spelled
#  out so the intent survives someone loosening a rule later.
*.pdf
*.apkg
*.docx
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gdoc
work/**
!work/.gitkeep
scripts/_out/
scripts/work/
scripts/__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
.pipeline_backups/
*.pyc
.DS_Store

# Build output. Generated icons, the staged payload, the frozen application
# and every installer are products, never sources.
build/
dist/
*.spec
*.icns
*.ico
*.dmg
*.exe
*.deb
*.AppImage

# Runtime JSON (including project_state.json and real audit records) stays out.
# Only publisher-owned templates/manifests are added back above.
